+  <div class="card">
+    <p class="eyebrow">Free two-minute check</p>
+    <h1>Coach, therapist, <em>or both?</em></h1>
+
+    <p class="lede">Both help. They help with different things. Picking the wrong one first is how people spend six months and decide help does not work for them.</p>
+    <p class="lede muted">This check takes two minutes. It tells you which one fits this month, in plain language, from a physician who will tell you when therapy is the better first step.</p>
+
+    <div class="rule"></div>
+    <p class="crisis">If you are having thoughts of harming yourself, call or text 988 (the Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline in the US) or go to the nearest emergency room. Please do not wait for a worksheet.</p>
+    <p class="kicker">What is inside</p>
+    <ul class="inside"><li>Eight quick pairs. Check the one that sounds like you</li><li>What your answers mean, and where to start</li><li>The difference between coaching and therapy, without jargon</li><li>Three questions to ask anyone before you book</li></ul>
+
+    <form id="signupForm" novalidate>
+      <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
+        <label for="company">Company</label>
+        <input type="text" id="company" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
+      </div>
+      <div class="field" id="firstNameField">
+        <label for="firstName">First name</label>
+        <input type="text" id="firstName" name="firstName" autocomplete="given-name" placeholder="First name">
+        <p class="field-error">Please enter your first name.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="field" id="emailField">
+        <label for="email">Email</label>
+        <input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" placeholder="you@email.com">
+        <p class="field-error">Please enter a valid email address.</p>
+      </div>
+      <button type="submit" class="cta" id="submitBtn">Send me the check</button>
+      <p class="cta-note">Free. You will also get the Sunday Letter. Unsubscribe any time.</p>
+      <div class="form-status" id="formStatus"></div>
+    </form>
+    <div class="done-box" id="doneBox">
+      <p>Your download has started. If it did not, <a href="#" id="againLink" style="color:var(--terracotta)">tap here to download Coach, Therapist, or Both</a>.</p>
+      <p class="next">Next step: Landed on coaching, or on both? <a href="/free-session">Book a free session</a>. 55 minutes, no pitch.</p>
+    </div>
+
+    <div class="rule"></div>
+
+    <div class="faq">
+      <h2>Questions people ask</h2>
+      <h3>What is the difference between a life coach and a therapist?</h3><p>Therapy diagnoses and treats mental health conditions, can work deeply with the past, and is done by a licensed clinician. Coaching looks forward. It works on decisions, direction, and action, and does not diagnose or treat. Therapy asks what is going on and where it came from. Coaching asks what you want and what is in the way.</p><h3>Should I see a coach or a therapist for burnout?</h3><p>It depends on what it looks like for you. If it is affecting your sleep, appetite, mood, or relationships most days, start with a therapist or your own doctor. If you are functioning but stuck on what to change, coaching can help. Many people use both.</p><h3>Can I see a coach and a therapist at the same time?</h3><p>Yes, and it is common. Tell each one about the other. They work on different parts of the same life.</p>
+    </div>
+
+    <div class="rule"></div>
+
+    <div class="bio">
+      <img src="/headshot.jpg" alt="Lauren Fine, MD">
+      <p><strong>Lauren Fine, MD</strong> is an allergist immunologist and a medical educator. She works with high achievers, in medicine and outside it, who are deciding whether to stay, scale back, or leave.</p>
+    </div>
+    <a class="cta" href="/free-session" style="margin-top:26px;background:var(--terracotta);">Book a free 55-minute session</a>
+    <p class="cta-note">A place to think out loud. No pitch.</p>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="foot"><a href="/resources">More free tools</a><a href="/about">About Lauren</a><a href="/">laurenfine.com</a></div>
+</div>
